<title>SINGAPORE: Nippecraft plunges to 1st-half loss.</title>
<headline>Nippecraft plunges to 1st-half loss.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				  4.62 vs   1.12 (profit)</p>
<p>    Group loss per share (cents)	2.30 vs   0.55 (profit)</p>
<p>    Turnover				 30.88 vs  33.55</p>
<p>    Operating profit			3.76 vs   3.46</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    1.87 vs   0.84</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	   1.23 vs   1.51</p>
<p>    Exceptional loss			5.48 vs    nil</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss		    3.82 vs    nil</p>
<p>Note - Stationery and diary publishers Nippecraft Ltd said the exceptional loss was a result of rationalisation and restructuring, including the write-down of stocks.</p>
<p>An extraordinary loss was due to the write-down of investments in and amounts due from a U.S. subsidiary that would be closed during the year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
